{"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"metadata":{"role":"collection","roleHeading":"Framework","modules":[{"name":"RecordsCalendarUI"}],"title":"RecordsCalendarUI","symbolKind":"module","externalID":"RecordsCalendarUI"},"sections":[],"topicSections":[{"anchor":"Calendar-Presentation","identifiers":["doc:\/\/recordscalendarui.RecordsCalendarUI\/documentation\/RecordsCalendarUI\/RecordsCalendarView","doc:\/\/recordscalendarui.RecordsCalendarUI\/documentation\/RecordsCalendarUI\/RecordsCalendarConfiguration","doc:\/\/recordscalendarui.RecordsCalendarUI\/documentation\/RecordsCalendarUI\/RecordsCalendarWeekTitleContext","doc:\/\/recordscalendarui.RecordsCalendarUI\/documentation\/RecordsCalendarUI\/RecordsCalendarTheme","doc:\/\/recordscalendarui.RecordsCalendarUI\/documentation\/RecordsCalendarUI\/RecordsCalendarDisplayScope"],"title":"Calendar Presentation"},{"anchor":"Record-Model-Boundary","identifiers":["doc:\/\/recordscalendarui.RecordsCalendarUI\/documentation\/RecordsCalendarUI\/RecordsCalendarEntry"],"title":"Record Model Boundary"},{"anchor":"Structures","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/recordscalendarui.RecordsCalendarUI\/documentation\/RecordsCalendarUI\/RecordsCalendarBestValueComparator","doc:\/\/recordscalendarui.RecordsCalendarUI\/documentation\/RecordsCalendarUI\/RecordsCalendarDayAccessibilityContext"],"title":"Structures"}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/recordscalendarui"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/recordscalendarui.RecordsCalendarUI\/documentation\/RecordsCalendarUI"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Reusable SwiftUI calendar records UI for apps that own their own data, persistence, and navigation."}],"kind":"symbol","primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"RecordsCalendarUI","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" provides presentation-only calendar components for record-based apps. Host apps pass records, display configuration, selection state, and callbacks while keeping storage and detail navigation outside the package.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Use this package when you need a reusable week\/month calendar with a selected-day list and swipe-to-delete behavior, but each app needs different record values, text formatting, and detail screens.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Week scope uses the display calendar’s locale and first weekday to create a localized year, month, and week-of-month header. A Korean calendar displays a title such as ","type":"text"},{"code":"2026년 7월 1주차","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" without host formatting, and the week number follows the visible calendar grid.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Built-in week-title localizations cover English, Simplified Chinese, Traditional Chinese, French, German, Italian, Japanese, Korean, Portuguese (Portugal), and Spanish. Other locales fall back to English.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Calendar navigation, week\/month scope changes, day selection, and record detail selection provide native haptic feedback. Tappable calendar and record surfaces also use a bouncy press response while respecting the Reduce Motion accessibility setting.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"RecordsCalendarConfiguration.rowHeight","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" controls the minimum selected-day row card height. ","type":"text"},{"code":"RecordsCalendarConfiguration.rowSpacing","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" controls the vertical spacing between selected-day rows, defaults to 5 points, can be customized by host apps, and clamps negative values to zero. Values below ","type":"text"},{"code":"RecordsCalendarConfiguration<YourRecord>.minimumRowHeight","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", currently 44 points, are clamped so row content keeps a standard touch target. Row spacing does not reduce the configured row height. ","type":"text"},{"code":"RecordsCalendarConfiguration<YourRecord>.minimumRowHeight(forRowSpacing:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" remains as a deprecated compatibility helper; use ","type":"text"},{"code":"minimumRowHeight","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" for new code.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"RecordsCalendarConfiguration.theme","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" accepts semantic colors through ","type":"text"},{"code":"RecordsCalendarTheme","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", including the full-page background, calendar and record container background, primary and secondary page content colors, optional container-only primary and secondary content colors, and independent light and dark summary tile backgrounds. The default ","type":"text"},{"code":".standard","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" theme preserves the system grouped page background, material calendar container, grouped record containers, and existing green appearance. Host apps can supply adaptive SwiftUI colors without changing package internals.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Theme initialization without an explicit light-mode secondary content color remains supported and derives that color from ","type":"text"},{"code":"contentColor","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"To change only surfaces, copy ","type":"text"},{"code":".standard","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and set ","type":"text"},{"code":"backgroundColor","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"code":"containerBackgroundColor","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". The package applies the container color consistently to the calendar, selected-day empty state, and record rows. Set ","type":"text"},{"code":"containerContentColor","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"containerSecondaryContentColor","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" when those containers need a foreground palette that differs from the page. Selected calendar days continue to use the page primary content color so it remains paired with ","type":"text"},{"code":"selectedDayBackgroundColor","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Calendar day buttons can receive an accessibility label and value from ","type":"text"},{"code":"RecordsCalendarConfiguration","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". The package passes a ","type":"text"},{"code":"RecordsCalendarDayAccessibilityContext","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" with the date, its display calendar, and the today, selected, and has-records states so host apps can provide their own localized full-date label and state text. Use ","type":"text"},{"code":"context.calendar","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" when formatting the date so its locale and time zone stay consistent with the visible calendar. When these closures are omitted, the package preserves SwiftUI’s default day-number announcement. Selected dates also use the system selected accessibility trait.","type":"text"}]}]}],"references":{"doc://recordscalendarui.RecordsCalendarUI/documentation/RecordsCalendarUI/RecordsCalendarWeekTitleContext":{"title":"RecordsCalendarWeekTitleContext","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"RecordsCalendarWeekTitleContext"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/recordscalendarui.RecordsCalendarUI\/documentation\/RecordsCalendarUI\/RecordsCalendarWeekTitleContext","role":"symbol","type":"topic","abstract":[],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"RecordsCalendarWeekTitleContext"}],"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/recordscalendarui\/recordscalendarweektitlecontext"},"doc://recordscalendarui.RecordsCalendarUI/documentation/RecordsCalendarUI/RecordsCalendarDayAccessibilityContext":{"abstract":[],"type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":